    text: "Baseline change 2026-07-15: files missing_linked_paths_total 162 -> 166 (moved 111 -> 116, deleted stable 50, orphaned 0). The +5 moved rows come from PR#565 relocating config/profile/init/template/extension engines into src/sdk ownership; closed lane items still link the old src/cli paths. Moved rows remain mechanical-relink territory per this item; CREATE-ONLY on closed holders (changelog drag)."
  - created_at: "2026-07-15T18:52:22.866Z"
    author: maintainer-agent
    text: "Baseline 2026-07-15 (post-PR#568): missing=168 = 118 moved + 50 deleted, orphaned=0. +2 moved vs pass #86 (166=116+50) from PR#568 SDK relocations (validate/health/gc engines moved to src/sdk/governance/, extension runtime split into install-runtime/install-snapshot/concurrency/update-check under src/sdk/extension/). Mechanical-relink class, no judgment rows added."
  - created_at: "2026-07-16T18:02:00.933Z"
    author: maintainer-agent
    text: "Files baseline moved 168 -> 172 on 2026-07-16 (pass #93): PR#573 SDK execution/diagnostics promotion relocated command internals; split now 121 moved (+3) + 51 deleted (+1), orphaned=0. Moved rows remain mechanical relink; the +1 deleted row needs judgment at burn-down."
  - created_at: "2026-07-28T10:37:05.607Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Ledger movement (2026-07-28 measurement): `missing` 168 → **179**, `orphaned` 0 → **2**.\n\nThe orphaned pair is the notable half, because orphaned had been driven to zero and is supposed to stay there — these are tracked test files that no item links:\n\n```\ntests/unit/extensions/extension-activation-atomicity.spec.ts\ntests/unit/scripts/release/package-sdk-contract-parity.spec.ts\n```\n\nBoth are recent arrivals (the SDK contract-parity gate and the activation-atomicity suite), so this is the same leak shape as the earlier orphaned excursions: a PR adds a spec and closes its item without a `pm test`/`pm files` link. Mechanical to repair — link each to the item whose work introduced it.\n\n`missing` continues to be dominated by the moved-vs-deleted split this item owns; the +11 since the pass-#88 count of 168 is consistent with continued `packages/pm-*` relocation churn (the sample is heavy with `packages/pm-*/extensions/*/index.js` and `runtime-loader.js` paths that no longer exist under those names). Worth re-running the moved/deleted classification before the next mechanical relink so the two classes do not drift back together.\n"
  - created_at: "2026-07-28T15:05:24.713Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Linked-path baseline re-measured 2026-07-28: missing 179, classified 121 moved and 58 deleted, up from 168 at pass-time in mid-July, and the split has shifted toward moved rather than deleted. The orphaned side is back to 0: two spec files added by PR#777 and PR#788 had no owning item and were linked this pass, extension-activation-atomicity.spec.ts to pm-4vwcvq and package-sdk-contract-parity.spec.ts to pm-vnk7ob, both attributed by git log --diff-filter=A on the file plus the pm ids in the introducing PR body. Both holders carry closed_at, so the links did not move their changelog sections. The recurrence pattern is now established: every PR that adds a spec without linking it reopens this warning class, which is the mechanical half this item owns."
  - created_at: "2026-07-29T04:34:39.701Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Measured 2026-07-29 while repairing this territory: the DATA half of this item is now zero on active holders. Thirteen stale links across pm-92if, pm-801d and pm-yh8r were repaired directly - six relocations (static-quality-gate.mjs to .mts, three governance-audit commands into packages/pm-governance-audit, extension doctor and item-filter-options into src/sdk) and seven removals of paths deleted upstream, including the sdk-import-boundary-baseline.json that pm-9x6e deleted when the ratchet became unconditional. What remains is 179 distinct paths held by 1,220 links across 472 holder items, every single one of them closed, so the residual is exactly the tracker-only migration this item scopes and nothing else. The REPORTING half - that the check warns regardless of holder lifecycle and truncates its worklist against a mislabelled denominator - is now owned by pm-zw9188; do not fold it back here."
  - created_at: "2026-07-30T17:16:29.708Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Census 2026-07-30 (evening), and it reframes this chore. The files check reports 179 missing linked paths against 1,383 linked project paths and 918 scanned candidates, classified by the tool itself as 121 moved and 58 deleted. Two orphaned paths were also reported and I cleared those by linking the two contract specs that shipped this afternoon to the items they prove, with runnable commands recorded, so the orphan count is zero.\n\nThe missing set is not dominated by relocations. Reading the reported sample by category: generated JavaScript siblings inside package extension folders, which are TypeScript-only sources by an accepted decision so the JavaScript never exists in a clean tree; generated example JavaScript under the docs tree; the generated changelog file; and one path under a temporary coverage output directory. Those are artifacts that are produced by a build or by a generator and are not tracked, so they are not missing in any meaningful sense. They were linked at a moment when a build had produced them.\n\nThat changes what closing this chore means. Repointing paths one by one treats every row as a relocation, and most rows are not. The durable fix has two halves. First, a link to a path that is generated or ignored should be refused at write time, the way a malformed link already is, because a link whose target is reconstructed by a build will break on every clean checkout and will keep this warning permanently non-zero. Second, the remaining genuine relocations are repaired with the in-place migrate flag rather than by remove and add, which preserves link notes.\n\nRecording the counts so the next pass can tell progress from noise: 179 missing, 1,383 linked, 918 candidates scanned, 121 classified moved, 58 classified deleted, 0 orphaned after this pass. If a later run shows the count falling while the generated-artifact categories remain, the wrong half was fixed."
  - created_at: "2026-08-03T11:21:11.612Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Live tracked-all file census 2026-08-03: 1,470 linked project paths and eight remote links were compared with 1,223 non-PM tracked candidate files. Validation reports 195 missing linked paths, classified as 140 moved and 55 deleted, plus 21 currently unowned tracked candidates. No links were pruned and no historical item was bulk-mutated; this canonical chore remains the evidence-batched owner."
