  "2026-07-06T08:22:48.232Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-06 audit #8 recount — pm validate now reports validate_files_missing_linked_paths 146 and validate_files_orphaned_paths 131 (workspace-wide, 2545 linked commands scanned). Counts unchanged in character since filing; still the single tracked owner of both warning classes."
  "2026-07-10T12:16:07.271Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-10 review pass: validate_files_missing_linked_paths rose 147 -> 154 (+7); orphaned_paths steady at 124. Likely cause: commits 21a7d884 (untracked vendored pm-changelog extension dist) and b573ef14 (contracts-snapshot gate rework) relocated/removed files still referenced by item linked paths. Worklist ids via pm validate --json .details.*_item_ids when picking this up."
  "2026-07-12T18:53:42.068Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-12 pass #74 delta: files_orphaned 123 -> 122 (PR#525 benchmark/scale tranche linked previously-orphaned paths); files_missing steady at 155 (pm-a2h3 annotation-command.ts delta from #73 unchanged). Baseline now 155/122."
  "2026-07-17T21:38:11.199Z",maintainer-agent,"Files baseline refresh (2026-07-17, post-PR#580 reconciliation) — missing=172 (121 moved / 51 deleted), was 168 (118m/50d) at the 2026-07-15 measurement. Delta = +3 moved +1 deleted from the PR#579/#580 sdk/graph + sdk/governance relocations on closed-item links. Orphaned went 0->3 transiently (PR#580 lane never file-linked analytics.ts + 2 specs) — repaired same day by linking all three to pm-7ob5; orphaned=0 again. Moved rows remain mechanical relink at execution; deleted rows judgment."
  "2026-07-19T11:19:40.301Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-19 baseline: missing_linked_paths 172 = 121 moved + 51 deleted (was 168 = 118+50 at the 2026-07-15 measurement); +3 moved +1 deleted from the PR#605/#614 relocation window. orphaned_paths 0 again — the six PR#614 files (merge.ts, sdk/merge/index.ts, four new sdk specs) were unlinked by the lane and are now linked to their shipping items (wc1r/9q2t/gpo7/cxyv/8xod). Classification native since validate ships moved/deleted counts."
  "2026-07-25T17:55:55.499Z","harness:claude-code","Files-baseline drift check 2026-07-25: `validate` reports `validate_files_missing_linked_paths:173`, against 168 recorded at the last measurement (2026-07-15) and 161 before that. Orphaned paths remain 0, so the drift is entirely on the missing side and the linking discipline for new work is holding.\n\nThe +5 since 2026-07-15 is consistent with continued source relocations (the SDK subpath moves and the packages/ boundary work both move files that closed items still link by their old path), not with new work failing to link. The classification split this item owns — mechanically relinkable moved rows versus judgment-required deleted rows — is what makes that distinction cheap to confirm, and it should be re-run before the next remediation batch so the moved half can be swept without touching the deleted half."
